{"id":"CVE-2012-0390","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2012-01-06T01:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T18:23:31.227Z","description":"The DTLS implementation in GnuTLS 3.0.10 and earlier executes certain error-handling code only if there is a specific relationship between a padding length and the ciphertext size, which makes it easier for remote attackers to recover partial plaintext via a timing side-channel attack, a related issue to CVE-2011-4108.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/57260","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"57260"},{"url":"http://www.isg.rhul.ac.uk/~kp/dtls.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2014-03/msg00001.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SU-2014:0320"}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2012-1569","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2012-03-26T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T19:01:02.196Z","description":"The asn1_get_length_der function in decoding.c in GNU Libtasn1 before 2.12, as used in GnuTLS before 3.0.16 and other products, does not properly handle certain large length values, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (heap memory corruption and application crash) or possibly have unspecified other impact via a crafted ASN.1 structure.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/57260","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"57260"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2012-0427.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2012:0427"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/48578","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"48578"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2012-0531.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2012:0531"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/49002","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"49002"},{"url":"http://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/package-announce/2012-April/077339.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2012-4357"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2012/03/20/8","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20120320 Re: CVE request: libtasn1 \"asn1_get_length_der()\" DER decoding issue"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2012/03/21/5","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20120321 Re: CVE request: GnuTLS TLS record handling issue / MU-201202-01"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/48488","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"48488"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-1436-1","tags":["vendor